    "created_at": "2018-01-21T20:40:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-21T20:42:03Z",
    "body": "Should be a \"bug\" if Spring would know that the connection is closed.\r\nBUT; \"EventSource.close()\" does NOT send anything to the server; so that, in the server-side, no-one will know a connection is closed by the client. That's the problem.\r\n\r\nIn fact, the problem is reported, to Spring-based apps, by Apache Tomcat, who rises the main exception server-side.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
