    "created_at": "2018-01-22T11:43:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-22T11:44:31Z",
    "body": "Tomcat, or any other web server, doesn't know that the client is no more there! The *application* code (Spring app) tries to send more messages and this fails with \"connection already closed\" error and then Tomcat releases its resources for this connection at the server side.\r\nSame might happen for any static resource - it the user navigates to another page while a static resource is still being served such kind of error will occur.\r\n\r\nIn this case a workaround might be to listen for `beforeunload` on the `window` and use `EventSource#close()` to notify the server.\r\n\r\nI am not sure whether the browsers should do this by default.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/359399845/reactions",
